From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:50:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backport: deps: Upgrade webrender to 0.70.1 (#49329)

The updated WebRender backports fixes for a regression, where on high
DPI displays servo would draw color bitmap emoji at 1/DPR of the
intended size. The same could also be observed when applying `transform:
scale()` to emoji.

The issue manifested slightly differently in Gecko, since Gecko
apparently builds display lists in device pixels. Servo however applies
a scale transform to get to device pixels
(https://github.com/servo/servo/blob/6d3c9c30951d019d997e364fee133669ba234679/components/paint/painter.rs#L674)

Testing: Testing DPR is not possible with the current servo testrunner.
Adding a reftest that uses scale might be possible, but since the
regression was covered by a wrench test in WebRender, I didn't try to
add one.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 988d63c306a3688229c4df45ea926f4ea57808cc)

----

Fork note: backported onto Servo v0.6.0 for the ohos-v0.6 branch. wr_glyph_rasterizer 0.70.1 also links the FreeType variation functions on OpenHarmony as on Android. With 0.70.0, ohos-main's OpenHarmony builds crashed on the `succeeded(res)` assertion in 113 of the 875 css-backgrounds tests on a DAYU200; the 2026-10-29 sync fixed that with a WebRender git pin first and then with this commit. Cargo.lock takes only the two WebRender versions: the change of one crate's syn dependency to 3.0.4 that came along upstream is left out, because v0.6.0 resolves that crate with syn 2 (`cargo metadata --locked` fails otherwise).

Validation: On the final stack, at its tip: `./mach test-tidy` (including cargo-deny), `./mach test-scripts`, `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, the crown build (checked-release, -D warnings, crown built for Rust 1.97.1), `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` with and without `--doc`, and the OpenHarmony checked-release builds of both flavors with -D warnings, which make signed HAPs, pass; release builds of it with both engines ran the whole WPT suite. On a DAYU200 with OpenHarmony 7.0, the stack's QuickJS headless checked-release executable ran /infrastructure, /css/css-backgrounds and /webstorage through `mach test-wpt --ohos` (1,098 tests in 31 minutes) without a crash in css-backgrounds; one webstorage quota test was reported crashed, as these tests crash under load on the host too. Before this fix, ohos-main's checked-release build crashed on FreeType's `succeeded(res)` assertion in 113 of 875 css-backgrounds tests.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent cherry-picked upstream commit 988d63c306a, left its syn change out of Cargo.lock and added the fork-style part of this message below the dashed line: fork note, Validation and these trailers)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
